---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import {Header,Footer} from '../../components/ui';
import ListeningDemo from '../../components/ListeningDemo';
import {getPracticeLanguages} from '../../lib/content';
import '../../styles/growth.css';
const french=getPracticeLanguages().find(l=>l.id==='fr')!;
---
<Base title="Minimal-Pair Practice After Reading Fluent Forever | MinimalPairs" description="Read Fluent Forever and want to start training your ear? Try minimal-pair audio, a free listening challenge and focused English, French or Spanish practice in your browser.">
 <Header/><main class="growth-page"><header class="growth-hero"><p class="eyebrow">FROM READING TO LISTENING</p><h1>Read Fluent Forever?<br/><em>Put your ears to work.</em></h1><p class="growth-lede">You understand why unfamiliar sounds matter. Now spend a few minutes actually distinguishing them—with the words hidden while you listen.</p><div class="growth-actions"><a class="button button-dark" href="#try">Try a listening round →</a><a href="/resources/minimal-pairs-without-anki">Prefer to practice without making flashcards?</a></div></header>
 <section class="growth-grid" id="try"><div><h2>Start with French <em>u and ou.</em></h2><p>In French, <strong>tu</strong> and <strong>tout</strong> differ in one vowel. A minimal pair makes that difference easier to compare.</p><p>In this exercise, A and B are your two references. X is a different word spoken in a different voice. Choose which reference shares X’s target sound.</p><p>You are practicing the sound category across examples, so memorizing one recording won’t be enough.</p><div class="growth-links"><a href="/challenge/ship-vs-sheep">Try English instead →</a><a href="/learn/fr-u-y">See the French examples →</a><a href="/spanish-minimal-pairs">Learning Spanish? Explore its sound contrasts →</a></div></div><ListeningDemo client:visible language={french} contrastId="fr-u-y"/></section>
 <section class="growth-section"><h2>A practical way to begin.</h2><div class="growth-steps"><article><h3>Find a sound to work on</h3><p>Take the free listening check or choose a contrast you already find confusing.</p></article><article><h3>Listen before you read</h3><p>Compare the references, match the new sound, and hear corrective feedback during practice.</p></article><article><h3>Return with fresh examples</h3><p>Change words and voices. Revisit the contrasts that were hard instead of only repeating the ones you know.</p></article></div><div class="growth-actions"><a class="button button-dark" href="/diagnostic/fr">Check my French listening →</a><a href="/diagnostic/en">Check my English listening →</a><a href="/diagnostic/es">Check my Spanish listening →</a></div></section>
 <section class="growth-section"><h2>Where MinimalPairs fits.</h2><p>Fluent Forever’s pronunciation materials introduce the idea of training your ear before relying on familiar spelling. MinimalPairs is an independent listening tool for practicing sound contrasts in your browser. It can sit alongside your book, tutor, vocabulary deck or other language course.</p><p>Choose sound matching with the words hidden, or word identification when you want to connect sounds to written words. Practice gives you feedback; the diagnostic saves feedback for your results.</p><p>Listening practice is one part of learning a language. Keep using conversation, reading and vocabulary work alongside it.</p><a href="/method">Read how the listening exercises work →</a></section>
 <section class="growth-price"><div><strong>One purchase. All current practice languages.</strong><p>$29 lifetime, or $7/month. The listening check and first three lessons in each language are free.</p></div><a class="button button-dark" href="/pricing">See what’s included →</a></section>
 <section class="growth-section"><h2>Questions before you start?</h2><details class="growth-question"><summary>Do I need Anki or a Fluent Forever account?</summary><p>No. Open an exercise in your browser. You can try the free lessons without an account.</p></details><details class="growth-question"><summary>Is this made by Fluent Forever?</summary><p>No. MinimalPairs is independent and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Fluent Forever.</p></details><details class="growth-question"><summary>Will I see which sounds I missed?</summary><p>The free diagnostic gives an overall score and a preview of your sound profile. Premium opens the detailed report and full practice library.</p></details><p class="growth-source">For the original pronunciation guidance, see <a href="https://blog.fluent-forever.com/chapter3/">Fluent Forever’s Chapter 3 resources</a> and <a href="https://blog.fluent-forever.com/learning-pronunciation/">its pronunciation article</a>.</p></section>
 </main><Footer/>
</Base>
